    "summary": "A long, quiet look at the birds you hear far more often than you see.",
    "story": "<p>You find owls with your ears and by looking down: a scatter of pellets, a splash of white on the bark. Then you look up very slowly.</p><p>I never use calls or bait. Every bird here was going about its day, and I left it to get on with it.</p>",
